WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.031 --> 00:00:11.331
The next time Pollyanna visited Mrs. Snow, the woman was lying in bed with the curtains closed.

2
00:00:11.332 --> 00:00:16.720
"I wish you'd come yesterday," Mrs. Snow said in an irritable voice.

3
00:00:16.721 --> 00:00:20.661
"I wanted you yesterday."

4
00:00:20.662 --> 00:00:26.168
"Then I'm glad I'm only a day late," Pollyanna said cheerfully.

5
00:00:26.169 --> 00:00:29.752
"It's awfully dark in here."

6
00:00:29.753 --> 00:00:32.901
Pollyanna crossed the room and opened the curtains.

7
00:00:32.902 --> 00:00:38.525
"I brought you a surprise and left it with Milly in the kitchen.

8
00:00:38.526 --> 00:00:44.076
I'll give you a hint—think of something you'd like."

9
00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:46.310
Mrs. Snow frowned.

10
00:00:46.311 --> 00:00:52.653
She was used to saying what she didn't want; she had no idea what she did want.

11
00:00:52.654 --> 00:00:55.213
"Chicken soup?"

12
00:00:55.214 --> 00:00:58.890
"I've got that," Pollyanna said.

13
00:00:58.891 --> 00:01:03.621
"No, I've changed my mind. Lamb stew."

14
00:01:03.622 --> 00:01:07.164
"I've got that and beef stew too!

15
00:01:07.165 --> 00:01:11.579
Nancy and I made them all, so you'd have something you like."

16
00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:14.429
Mrs. Snow didn't know how to respond.

17
00:01:14.430 --> 00:01:19.046
But that wasn't a problem because Pollyanna went right on talking.

18
00:01:19.047 --> 00:01:23.453
"I've played the game and found something for you to be glad about.

19
00:01:23.454 --> 00:01:27.123
It was extra hard because you have to stay in bed.

20
00:01:27.124 --> 00:01:31.278
But the game is even more fun when it's hard."

21
00:01:31.279 --> 00:01:36.073
"What game?" Mrs. Snow was puzzled.

22
00:01:36.074 --> 00:01:40.597
"Wait!" Pollyanna took a deep breath.

23
00:01:40.598 --> 00:01:46.416
"You can be glad that other people aren't as sick as you are!"

24
00:01:46.417 --> 00:01:53.310
"Well, really!" Mrs. Snow was angry now, but Pollyanna was happily unaware of that.

25
00:01:53.311 --> 00:02:00.364
"I'll tell you about the Glad Game." Pollyanna told the story of wanting a doll but receiving crutches instead.

26
00:02:00.365 --> 00:02:05.695
Just then Milly came in to announce that Miss Polly wanted Pollyanna to hurry home.

27
00:02:05.696 --> 00:02:09.653
"All right." Pollyanna sighed.

28
00:02:09.654 --> 00:02:13.245
"I'll hurry." Suddenly she laughed.

29
00:02:13.246 --> 00:02:18.169
"I guess I'm glad I have legs to hurry with!"

30
00:02:18.170 --> 00:02:26.813
Mrs. Snow didn't respond, but Milly noticed there were tears on her mother's cheeks.

31
00:02:26.814 --> 00:02:32.783
*** Although it was raining the next time Pollyanna saw the man, she greeted him with a bright

32
00:02:32.784 --> 00:02:36.842
smile. He didn't even bother to grunt in

33
00:02:36.843 --> 00:02:42.534
response. Pollyanna assumed he had trouble hearing, so she spoke more loudly the next

34
00:02:42.535 --> 00:02:47.281
day. "I'm glad the sun is shining today, aren't

35
00:02:47.282 --> 00:02:50.765
you?" Pollyanna bent down to pat the dog with the

36
00:02:50.766 --> 00:02:56.974
man. The man scowled at her. "I've got other things to think about besides the weather.

37
00:02:56.975 --> 00:03:01.307
I don't know whether the sun is shining or not."

38
00:03:01.308 --> 00:03:03.376
Pollyanna smiled brightly.

39
00:03:03.377 --> 00:03:08.232
"That's exactly why I mentioned the sun—so you'd notice it!

40
00:03:08.233 --> 00:03:13.300
I knew you'd be glad about the sunshine if you stopped to think about it."

41
00:03:13.301 --> 00:03:17.969
The man started to walk away but abruptly turned around to face her again.

42
00:03:17.970 --> 00:03:22.363
"Why don't you find someone your own age to talk to?"

43
00:03:22.364 --> 00:03:27.142
"I'd like to, sir, but there's nobody my age around right now.

44
00:03:27.143 --> 00:03:32.157
And I like old folks. You see, I'm used to the Ladies' Aid—"

45
00:03:32.158 --> 00:03:39.900
"The Ladies' Aid? Is that what you thought I was?" The man was trying not to smile.

46
00:03:39.901 --> 00:03:47.292
Pollyanna laughed gleefully. "Oh no, sir! You don't look at all like a Ladies' Aider.

47
00:03:47.293 --> 00:03:51.798
In fact, I'm sure you're much nicer than you look."

48
00:03:51.799 --> 00:03:57.943
"What?" The man strode away.

49
00:03:57.944 --> 00:04:02.792
But the next time they met, the man spoke to Pollyanna before she could greet him.

50
00:04:02.793 --> 00:04:08.753
"Good afternoon! Perhaps I should say right away that I know the sun's shining."

51
00:04:08.754 --> 00:04:12.650
"I knew you knew it as soon as I saw you.

52
00:04:12.651 --> 00:04:16.833
I could see it in your eyes and your smile."

53
00:04:16.834 --> 00:04:20.021
"Humph!" grunted the man.

54
00:04:20.022 --> 00:04:24.390
But he continued to talk to Pollyanna whenever they met.

55
00:04:24.391 --> 00:04:31.434
One day Nancy happened to be with Pollyanna when the man greeted her.

56
00:04:31.435 --> 00:04:37.693
"Did that man just speak to you?" Nancy's eyes were wide with amazement.

57
00:04:37.694 --> 00:04:41.540
"He hasn't spoken to anyone for years."

58
00:04:41.541 --> 00:04:45.758
"He speaks to me, but he's never told me his name."

59
00:04:45.759 --> 00:04:52.011
"That's John Pendleton, and he lives by himself in a mansion on Pendleton Hill.

60
00:04:52.012 --> 00:04:57.394
Few people have ever seen inside his house because he doesn't like visitors.

61
00:04:57.395 --> 00:05:01.912
He's the richest man in town but doesn't like to spend his money."

62
00:05:01.913 --> 00:05:07.445
"Maybe he's saving it for orphans overseas or something," Pollyanna said.

63
00:05:07.446 --> 00:05:09.738
"I doubt it." Nancy went on.

64
00:05:09.739 --> 00:05:13.248
"Everybody thinks he's mysterious.

65
00:05:13.249 --> 00:05:20.016
Some years he spends most of his time traveling to faraway places like Egypt."

66
00:05:20.017 --> 00:05:22.768
"He's different," Pollyanna said.

67
00:05:22.769 --> 00:05:26.633
"But a different kind of different than Mrs. Snow.

68
00:05:26.634 --> 00:05:32.960
I'm gladder than ever that he speaks to me now!"

